    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d910">

                <pb facs="1337" n="1323" sameAs="frus:frus1948v06/pg1323"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Korea)/11–948: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Special Representative in Korea</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Muccio</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Seoul</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-11-09">November 9,
                        1948</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>194. Cite Zpol 1876. Pass Paris GADel for Jacobs.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d910-f1"/>
                    Following message from President Rhee to Chang Myun, Korean delegation Paris:
                    “Due to recent uprising and also to continued propaganda stories coming from
                    north, people feel nervous for fear that Red Army might march down south moment
                    the American forces pull out. If necessary make formal appeal to UN Assembly to adopt resolution requesting US to
                    retain even a token force in south for time being”.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Muccio</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d910-f1" n="1" xml:id="d910-f1-content">
                <p>This was done the same day.</p>
            </note>
